        "caseStudy": {
          "overview": "A group project for the System Analysis & Design capstone. The team models how a bank can detect and investigate fraudulent transactions, starting from a list of functional requirements.",
          "role": "I modeled four cases from the Actor's point of view: Initiate Card Payment, Analyze Transactions Using AI, Review Suspicious Transactions and Create Fraud Investigation Case. I also drew the Fraud Analyst and System Administrator block diagrams.",
          "approach": "Each case became an Activity diagram and a State diagram, then Sequence diagrams and Level 1 Data Flow Diagrams, all tied together by one Use Case diagram.",
          "challenges": "Keeping every decision to a single condition, starting conditions with a verb, and making loop-backs return to where the flow came from.",
          "outcome": "Use Case, Activity, State and Block diagrams were submitted for Performance 2 with a cover page.",
          "tech": [
